  "notes": "Yamamoto-first discovery pass on 2026-08-29 under the current durable repository authority. docs/PRIORITIES.md, docs/EDITORIAL.md, docs/DOMAINS.md, radar/inbox/README.md, and the current merge contract were consulted before grading or publication. Fresh checks of Jazz House ALFIE, BODY&SOUL, Tsuyoshi Yamamoto schedule traces, Space M&A, and credible Japanese-jazz sources did not produce a new verified unrecorded Yamamoto performance with enough event-specific context to clear RADAR admission; recurring Space M&A trio dates were not admitted merely because Yamamoto is present. Two broader discoveries clear Stage 1 for performance-specific reasons. Takeo Moriyama 2DAYS is A+ because the current twin-sax/vibraphone/bass quintet gives a living master of Japanese jazz a strong present-tense instrumental identity in PIT INN; two nights and Moriyama's continuing activity make A+ sufficient without manufacturing scarcity. Marsalis' Swinging Cities is A because the three-suite city/cultural-exchange program gives the concert a specific editorial argument during Marsalis's final season as JALC Artistic Director, while two performances and a season full of Marsalis-led programs make it useful to know rather than a night that should dominate travel. Proposed shape A 1 / A+ 1 / S 0 / S+ 0 is consistent with the current/recent RADAR pattern of an A/A+ base and rare scarcity tiers.",
