      "editorial": {
        "en": {
          "why_it_matters": "The current quintet is the reason, not Moriyama's history alone: twin saxophones and vibraphone sit over Sugawa's bass and Moriyama's drums, giving one of the defining drummers of Japan's post-1960s jazz lineage a colorful present-tense small-group sound at PIT INN. The instrumentation also echoes the reed-and-rhythm openness long associated with Moriyama without pretending this is a retrospective program.",
